# Publishing

For now, these packages are local only and aren't hosted anywhere.

To create a new version of the packages and publish, run:

```bash
# Package
dotnet pack .\analyzers\Dward.Analyzers\Dward.Analyzers.csproj -c Release -o .\artifacts\packages
dotnet pack .\analyzers\Dward.Godot.Analyzers\Dward.Godot.Analyzers.csproj -c Release -o .\artifacts\packages

# Publish
dotnet nuget push .\artifacts\packages\Dward.Analyzers.1.0.0.nupkg --source DwardLocal
dotnet nuget push .\artifacts\packages\Dward.Godot.1.0.0.nupkg --source DwardLocal
```

# Testing

In addition to the actual .NET tests, there is also a Python script that creates temporary .NET projects to verify the analyzers and code fixes all load and works as expected.

```bash
# .NET tests
dotnet test .\analyzers\Dward.Analyzers.sln

# Tests for the python and gdscript validation scripts
$env:GODOT_PATH = 'C:\Users\dward\scoop\shims\godot-mono.exe'
python -m unittest discover -s .\analyzers\Dward.Godot.Analyzers\tools\tests -v

# Run the Python verifier script
python -m unittest discover -s .\analyzers\tests -v


```